      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum single dose of about 1,000 mg. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Possible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg or 850 mg twice daily, if the patient is starting metformin\n\nPlease tell me the dose you intended. If 1700 mg three times daily is deliberate, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note."
